# zentone: ACES 2.0 Output Transform strip kernel — 16x faster than per-pixel scalar
date:   2026-08-28
host:   Apple M4 Pro (12 core), macOS, aarch64 (NEON tier; f32x8 = 2 x f32x4)
build:  release, NO -C target-cpu=native
commit: (the commit adding src/experimental/aces2_simd.rs; see git log)
cmd:    cargo bench --bench pipeline_bench --features experimental
        (groups aces2_sdr_rec709 / aces2_hdr_rec2020; full log ~/tmp/zentone-bench-aces2.log)
input:  PQ ramp strip fed to `pipeline::tonemap_pq_row_simd` with the transform
        as the curve — "scalar" = trait default per-pixel `forward` via a
        ScalarFallback wrapper, "simd" = `map_strip_simd` override
        (`experimental::aces2_simd::aces2_forward_tier`). Same fused PQ outer
        kernel on both sides, so the delta is the transform alone.

## Results (zenbench, mean ± MAD)

  group              width   scalar        simd        speedup   simd ns/px
  aces2 100nit 709    256    234.2 µs     14.3 µs     16.4x     56
  aces2 100nit 709   1024    925.1 µs     56.5 µs     16.4x     55
  aces2 100nit 709   4096   3704.9 µs    224.6 µs     16.5x     55
  aces2 1000nit 2020  256    214.0 µs     14.4 µs     14.9x     56
  aces2 1000nit 2020 1024    852.5 µs     56.7 µs     15.0x     55
  aces2 1000nit 2020 4096   3403.6 µs    226.6 µs     15.0x     55

Scalar: ~0.83-0.91 µs per pixel (libm powf x ~14, atan2, sin, cos, sqrt,
per-pixel hue-table search). SIMD: ~55 ns per pixel, flat across widths
(no per-call fixed cost visible at 256 px: 14.3 µs / 256 = 56 ns).

The remaining per-lane scalar work in the kernel is the hue-table gather
(reach M lerp + interval search + cusp/gamma lerps) — 8 scalar lookups per
chunk. It was left single-sourced with the scalar transform on purpose.

## Accuracy

SIMD vs scalar forward: worst 1.1e-4 normalised error (|d| / (1 + |want|))
over the 4 golden configurations x (296 golden inputs + 1000 log-uniform
random + 100 slightly-negative + 7 hostile) — pinned by
`aces2_simd::tests::strip_matches_scalar` (bound 2e-4 abs + 2e-4 rel,
worst <= 1.5e-4). The kernel also passes the OpenColorIO forward golden
(1e-3 + 1e-3 rel) directly. Not bit-identical: magetypes pow_midp /
log2_midp / exp2_midp plus in-kernel minimax atan2 / sincos replace libm.
